      "message": "USDOT needs FEAT_I8MM, which is a strictly stronger requirement than this file\u0027s FEAT_DotProd baseline -- Neoverse N1, which is what the numbers in this commit are measured on, has DotProd but not I8MM, so a USDOT version dropped into this neon_dotprod specialization would SIGILL there. I don\u0027t currently have access to i8mm-capable hardware to implement and verify it properly (bit-exact + a real benchmark, not just a compile check), so I\u0027d rather not land something I can\u0027t test to the same standard as the rest of this series. I think this wants a separate av1_resize_horz_dir variant in the existing resize_neon_i8mm.c as a follow-up once I do -- happy to pick it up then, or if you\u0027d rather see it land as part of this series I can look into getting access sooner.",
